---
title: Apple Dumplings
source: Grandma Schwennesen
---

Grease a #13x9 inch pan{} and set aside.

In a #pan{} over medium heat, melt @butter{2%sticks} and stir in @brown sugar{1-1/2%cups} and @vanilla{1/2%tsp}.

Peel and core @apples{2} into 8 pieces each.

Open @crescent rolls{2%packages} and separate into triangles.

Roll a piece of apple into each crescent triangle and place on the greased pan.

Spoon the melted butter and brown sugar mixture over each dumpling. Sprinkle @cinnamon{1%tsp} over the top.

Pour @lemon-lime soda{12%oz} along the sides of the pan and in between the dumplings, but NOT ON THE DUMPLINGS.

Bake at 350 F for ~{35%minutes}.
